.TH WIILANDD 1 "August 2026" "wiiland" "WiiLand Manual"
.SH NAME
wiilandd \- bridge Wii Remote input to Linux virtual evdev devices
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wiilandd
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.br
.B wiilandd --device
.I number-or-absolute-path
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B wiilandd
reads Linux hid-wiimote events through the native wiiland-hid device library
and exposes the selected Wii Remote inputs through Linux
.BR uinput .
The resulting devices are named
.B "WiiLand Virtual Controller"
and
.B "WiiLand Virtual Desktop"
and are consumed through the normal evdev/libinput path.  The daemon does not
connect to a display server.
.PP
With no action option, the daemon monitors all connected and hot-plugged
remotes.  With
.BR --device ,
it handles one selected remote.  A selector is a positive ordinal from
.BR --list
or an absolute device path (normally below
.BR /sys ).
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
Value options accept either a separate value (for example,
.B --profile desktop
) or an equals form (for example,
.BR --profile=desktop ).
The optional value of
.B --trace-events
is supplied only in the equals form.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Print command help and exit.  This mode does not load configuration.
.TP
.B --version
Print the version and exit.  This mode does not load configuration.
.TP
.BR -l , " --list"
List connected Wii Remotes and exit.  Each device is printed as an ordinal,
a tab, and its sysfs path.  If no devices are found, print
.B "No Wii Remote devices found"
\&.  Combine with
.BR --verbose
to print
.B devtype
and
.B extension
attributes for each device.
.TP
.BR -d , " --device " number-or-absolute-path
Handle one device instead of monitoring all devices.  An ordinal is resolved
in monitor order; an absolute path is used as supplied.  This option also
selects the device for
.BR --calibrate-aim .
.TP
.BR -p , " --profile " gamepad\fR|\fBdesktop\fR|\fBboth
Select the default virtual-input profile.  The default is
.BR gamepad .
.B desktop
adds pointer and desktop button output;
.B both
enables both profiles.  Per-device configuration rules can override this
selection.
.TP
.B --backend=uinput
Select the input backend.  The only accepted value and the default is
.BR uinput .
.TP
.B --pointer-speed=1-127
Desktop D-pad pointer step per repeat tick.  The default is 16.
.TP
.B --ir-speed=1-127
Desktop IR pointer gain.  The default is 8.
.TP
.B --ir-deadzone=0-127
Discard small IR pointer deltas after gain scaling.  The default is 0.
.TP
.B --ir-smoothing=0-95
Retain this percentage of the previous filtered IR position.  The default is
0.
.TP
.B --ir-tracking=dual\fR|\fBcentroid\fR|\fBfirst
Select the IR source tracker.  The default is
.BR dual ,
which uses the midpoint of the widest valid pair;
.B centroid
averages valid points, and
.B first
uses the first valid point.
.TP
.B --ir-aim-mapping=relative\fR|\fBabsolute
Select IR aim output mapping.  The default is
.BR relative .
.B absolute
uses the
.B ir-screen-*
configuration bounds.
.TP
.B --aim-mode=off\fR|\fBmouse\fR|\fBright-stick
Select motion aim output.  The default is
.BR off .
.B mouse
emits relative pointer motion and
.B right-stick
emits ABS_RX/ABS_RY aim axes.
.TP
.B --aim-source=auto\fR|\fBir\fR|\fBmotion-plus\fR|\fBaccelerometer
Select the motion sensor for aim.  The default is
.BR auto ,
which prefers IR, then MotionPlus, then accelerometer data.
.TP
.B --aim-activation=always\fR|\fBb\fR|\fBz\fR|\fBc
Select aim activation.  The default is
.BR b .
The latter three values gate aim on the Wii Remote B, Nunchuk Z, or Nunchuk C
button respectively.
.TP
.B --aim-sensitivity=1-127
Motion aim gain.  The default is 16.
.TP
.B --aim-deadzone=0-32767
Motion aim deadzone before gain.  The default is 4.
.TP
.B --aim-smoothing=0-95
Motion aim smoothing percentage.  The default is 25.
.TP
.B --aim-invert-x=yes\fR|\fBno
Invert motion aim X.  The default is
.BR no .
Values
.BR true / false
and
.BR 1 / 0
are also accepted.
.TP
.B --aim-invert-y=yes\fR|\fBno
Invert motion aim Y.  The default is
.BR no .
Values
.BR true / false
and
.BR 1 / 0
are also accepted.
.TP
.B --aim-calibration-duration=1-30
Number of seconds sampled by
.BR --calibrate-aim .
The default is 8.
.TP
.BR -c , " --config " path
Load one required key=value configuration file instead of the default layer
hierarchy.  Command-line values override the file.
.TP
.B --no-config
Use built-in defaults and do not load configuration files.  This option cannot
be combined with
.BR --config .
.TP
.BR -n , " --dry-run"
Run device handling without creating virtual uinput devices or emitting input.
.TP
.B --check-config
Load configuration, apply command-line values, validate it, and exit without
enumerating devices.
.TP
.B --dump-config
Print the resolved configuration as key=value lines and exit.  The output
reflects loaded files followed by command-line overrides.
.TP
.B --axis-map
Print the virtual gamepad axis and button map and exit.  This diagnostic does
not load configuration or enumerate devices.
.TP
.B --validation-checklist
Print the hardware-validation checklist and exit.  This diagnostic does not
load configuration or enumerate devices.
.TP
.B --doctor
Print environment, display-socket, configuration-path, and /dev/uinput
readiness fields and exit.  It loads configuration like a normal start unless
.B --no-config
is used.
.TP
.B --self-test
Run deterministic mapping, configuration, calibration, and trace checks, then
exit without enumerating devices or opening /dev/uinput.
.TP
.B --trace-events[=all\fR|\fBkeys\fR|\fBaxes\fR|\fBir\fR|\fBmotion-plus]
Enable decoded event records on standard output.  With no value the filter is
.B all
\&.  A value is supplied with an equals sign.  Records contain
.B time= ,
.B seq= ,
the sysfs path, event name and numeric type, followed by key state or
.B absN=x,y,z
payload fields.  Combine with
.B --dry-run
to observe events without virtual output.
.TP
.B --calibrate-aim
Sample a flat, stationary Wii Remote and print complete key=value calibration
lines for any stable accelerometer and MotionPlus sources.  If no
.B --device
is supplied, ordinal 1 is selected.  At least one stable source is required;
unstable or unavailable sources produce a warning.
.TP
.BR -v , " --verbose"
Print device lifecycle details.  With
.BR --list ,
also print each device's devtype and extension attributes.
.PP
At most one action may be selected.  Actions include
.BR --help ,
.BR --version ,
.BR --list ,
.BR --axis-map ,
.BR --validation-checklist ,
.BR --doctor ,
.BR --dump-config ,
.BR --check-config ,
.BR --self-test ,
and
.BR --calibrate-aim .
Conflicting actions and malformed or unknown options are rejected before an
action runs.
.TP
.B --ipc-socket PATH
Enable the private daemon IPC socket at the required absolute Unix-socket
path.  The parent directory is created privately when absent; binding
failures, including a live or unsafe existing path, are fatal.  This option
overrides the automatic socket path.  It conflicts with
.BR --no-ipc .
.TP
.B --no-ipc
Disable the private daemon IPC socket.  This option conflicts with
.BR --ipc-socket .
Without either option, IPC is automatic only when
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is set to an absolute path.
.PP
.SH IPC
The daemon IPC transport is a private per-user Unix stream socket carrying
newline-delimited UTF-8 JSON.  The normative version-1 wire protocol,
including framing, requests, responses, notifications, and compatibility
rules, is documented in
.BR DAEMON_PROTOCOL ,
normally installed as
.BR /usr/share/doc/wiiland/DAEMON_PROTOCOL .
The default path is
.BR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wiiland/wiilandd.sock .
Automatic mode does not create a socket when
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
is missing or relative.  An explicit
.B --ipc-socket
path must be absolute and binding errors are fatal.
.PP
The socket parent is mode 0700 and the socket is mode 0600; both must be owned
by the daemon's effective user.  An existing live socket is never taken over.
Only a stale socket with the same observed inode is removed, and shutdown
unlinks only the inode bound by this daemon.  There is no socket activation,
installed socket, C ABI, or installed client interface.
.PP
Protocol minor 1 adds diagnostics, running configuration, and sensor capture
leases. Captures are connection-owned and share interfaces across clients.
Stopping a capture or disconnecting releases its leases; profile-required
interfaces remain open. Diagnostic-only sensor reports do not feed virtual
input. Existing protocol major 1 commands and message shapes remain supported.
.PP
Trace and lifecycle output use bounded background queues. A slow output reader
can cause diagnostic records to be dropped, but cannot block input ingestion.
The diagnostics command exposes queue-loss counts and maximum pointer lateness
and dispatch duration. Writer shutdown waits at most 100 ms per stream.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration files contain one
.B key=value
entry per line.  A
.B #
starts a comment; values are not shell-expanded.  Numeric ranges and choice
values are validated, and lines are limited to 511 bytes.
.PP
Unless
.B --no-config
is used, the default hierarchy reads the optional system file first and the
optional user file second.  The fixed system path is
.BR /etc/wiiland/wiilandd.conf .
The user path is
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is absolute; otherwise, when HOME is absolute, it is
.B $HOME/.config/wiiland/wiilandd.conf .
Later values replace earlier values.  An explicit
.B --config
file is required and is loaded alone.  Help, version, list, axis-map, and
validation-checklist use built-in defaults without reading files.
.PP
The accepted keys are:
.TP
.B backend=uinput
The only supported input backend.
.TP
.B profile=gamepad|desktop|both
Default profile; the default is
.BR gamepad .
.TP
.B pointer-speed=1-127 , ir-speed=1-127 , ir-deadzone=0-127 , ir-smoothing=0-95
Desktop pointer and IR settings.  Defaults are 16, 8, 0, and 0 respectively.
.TP
.B ir-tracking=dual|centroid|first
IR tracker; default
.BR dual .
.TP
.B ir-aim-mapping=relative|absolute
IR aim mapping; default
.BR relative .
.TP
.B ir-screen-left=0-32767 , ir-screen-right=0-32767 , ir-screen-top=0-32767 , ir-screen-bottom=0-32767
Optional bounds for absolute IR aim.  Right must exceed left and bottom must
exceed top.
.TP
.B aim-mode=off|mouse|right-stick
Motion aim output; default
.BR off .
.TP
.B aim-source=auto|ir|motion-plus|accelerometer
Motion sensor; default
.BR auto .
.TP
.B aim-activation=always|b|z|c
Activation gate; default
.BR b .
.TP
.B aim-sensitivity=1-127 , aim-deadzone=0-32767 , aim-smoothing=0-95
Motion aim tuning.  Defaults are 16, 4, and 25.
.TP
.B aim-invert-x=yes|no , aim-invert-y=yes|no
Motion aim inversion.  Both default to
.BR no ;
.BR true / false
and
.BR 1 / 0
are accepted.
.TP
.B aim-accel-zero-x|y|z=-32768-32767
Complete accelerometer neutral triple.  A partial triple is invalid.
.TP
.B aim-motion-plus-bias-x|y|z=-32768-32767
Complete MotionPlus bias triple.  A partial triple is invalid.
.TP
.B aim-calibration-duration=1-30
Calibration sample duration in seconds; default is 8.
.TP
.B desktop.a|b|plus|minus|home|one|two=ACTION
Desktop button actions.  ACTION is one of
.BR disabled ,
.BR left-click ,
.BR right-click ,
.BR enter ,
.BR escape ,
.BR overview ,
.BR page-up ,
or
.BR page-down .
Defaults are left-click, right-click, enter, escape, overview, page-down, and
page-up for A, B, +, -, Home, 1, and 2 respectively.
.TP
.B device.<substring>.profile=gamepad|desktop|both
Apply a profile when the device sysfs path contains
.BR <substring> .
.TP
.B device-type.<substring>.profile=gamepad|desktop|both
Apply a profile when the hid-wiimote device type contains
.BR <substring> .
Rules are evaluated in file order and later matching rules win.  At most 32
rules are accepted.
.SH EXIT STATUS
A successful action returns zero.  Syntax, conflicting actions, configuration,
monitor, device, and runtime failures return a nonzero errno-style status.
The normal daemon action runs until stopped or until its runtime fails.
.SH HARDWARE REPORT
.B wiilandd-hardware-report
is an installed companion command.  With no arguments it emits a finite,
line-oriented schema-v2 report.  Its top-level sections, in order, are
.BR host ,
.BR permissions ,
.BR wiilandd ,
.BR devices ,
.BR manual-validation ,
and
.BR result .
Each section begins with
.B == SECTION ==
and most records are
.B key=value
lines.  The host section starts with
.B report.schema.version=2
and
.B report.timestamp.utc= .
The result section always contains
.B report.core-failures=
and
.B report.status=ok
or
.BR report.status=failed .
Core probe failures are numbered as
.B core.failure.N=...
; optional probe failures are reported as unavailable fields and do not by
themselves fail the report.  A device selector adds a
.B trace
section and replaces the report process with
.B wiilandd --dry-run --trace-events --verbose --device ... --profile both
plus non-conflicting forwarded arguments.  Stop that live capture with
.BR Ctrl-C .
.SH PERMISSIONS
The daemon must be able to read hid-wiimote input nodes and write
.BR /dev/uinput .
The daemon does not elevate privileges; use the system's normal udev ACL or
input/uinput group policy.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
Canonical installed system configuration path.
.TP
.B $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
Optional per-user configuration when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is absolute.
.TP
.B $HOME/.config/wiiland/wiilandd.conf
Fallback per-user configuration when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is unset or relative.
.TP
.B /dev/uinput
Kernel uinput device used by the daemon.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wiiland-config (1),
.BR wiiland-show (1),
.BR wiiland (7)
